 # bench-interpreters-card (benchmark fixture)
 
-An interpreter-path tool plugin: the host half registers `run_python` /
-`run_node` tools and exposes the `interpreters` config through a self-hosted
-`/interpreters/api` HTTP gateway route (reads/writes the settings namespace
-in-process through the settings bridge); the browser half registers a
-settings-plugins card that reads/writes through that route and converges on
-pushed connection invalidations. Written in the 0.1.1-era style. The host is
-moving to dsh 0.1.2-alpha.2.
+An interpreter-path tool plugin on the dsh 0.1.2-alpha.2 cohort: the host half
+registers `run_python` / `run_node` tools and exposes the `interpreters` config
+through its self-hosted `/interpreters/api` HTTP gateway route (the handler
+reads/writes the settings namespace in-process through the settings bridge,
+with the `cordis.patch.yml` entry as the namespace's base layer); the browser
+half registers a settings-plugins card into the harness-declared keyed
+`settings.plugin.item` slot, reads/writes that config through the same route,
+and converges on pushed `connection/reset` invalidations.
+
+The gateway route is the plugin's own entry point, not a stand-in for the
+official settings page: it keeps its JSON envelope
+(`{ ok: true, value: { config } }` | `{ ok: false, error }`) and its documented
+degrade — with no settings provider mounted, `get` falls back to the
+composition config and `set` answers a clear error. On this release the route
+runs behind the Connection browser-trust gate
+(`ctx.connection.requestRejection`) and is registered only while that gate is
+composed.
+
+Migrated from the 0.1.1-era form: the snapshot-store type surface moved from
+the removed `dsh-client-runtime` to `dsh-client-store`, the `dsh-settings`
+`Settings` type became `SettingsProvider`, the `webServer` service rename is in
+place, and the config gateway was rebased onto the alpha.2 auth gate instead of
+being retired behind the official settings surface (that surface serves
+registered namespaces, not `/interpreters/api`).
+
+Two packaging facts belong to the same move. The browser half ships as the
+client module system's lazy-CJS factory artifact
+(`window.__ModuleLoader__.load({ id, factory })`): alpha.2 concatenates every
+plugin bundle into one classic script, so a raw ESM half is a SyntaxError that
+fails the whole client combo, and the registration id must equal the package
+name. No published preset emits the artifact, so it is hand-rolled (tracked
+upstream in `.dsh-migrate/patch-reports/publish-client-bundle-preset/`). And
+`@deepseek-ai/schemastery` is a runtime dependency, not a peer: the host half
+validates its settings section with it, so the install has to provide it.
 
 Release procedure (internal):
 
